<title>USA: Snyder Oil Corp sells $175 mln in junk bonds.</title>
<headline>Snyder Oil Corp sells $175 mln in junk bonds.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following 144A private placement of high-yield debt from Snyder Oil Corp was priced on Thursday via NationsBanc Securities Inc, according to a market source.</p>
<p>The deal was increased from an original size of $150 million.</p>
<p>Snyder Oil, headquartered in Fort Worth, Texas, is an oil and gas exploration and production company.</p>
<p>BORROWER SNYDER OIL CORP</p>
<p>AMT $175 MLN</p>
<p>TYPE SR SUB NOTES</p>
<p>MATURITY 6/15/07</p>
<p>COUPON 8 3/4 PCT</p>
<p>ISS PRICE 99.179</p>
<p>YIELD 8.875 PCT</p>
<p>SPREAD +225 BPS</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S B2</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P B-PLUS</p>
<p>FIRST PAY DATE 12/15/97</p>
<p>PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>CALLABLE NON CALLABLE FOR FIVE YEARS</p>
<p>NOTE: THREE YEAR EQUITY CALL FOR 30 PERCENT OF THE ISSUE AT</p>
<p>108.75</p>
<p>((U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212 859-1662))</p>
</text>
